{"case_id": "bench-016", "set": "synthetic-bench", "category": "technical_extension", "provenance": "synthetic", "post_title": "A rate limiter in forty lines of Go", "parent": null, "reply_to_author": false, "body_html": "<p>We did something similar with a leaky bucket in Lua inside Redis, which keeps the check and the decrement atomic:</p><pre class=\"highlight lua\"><code>local n = redis.call('DECR', KEYS[1])\nreturn n &gt;= 0\n</code></pre>", "body_source_format": "HTML", "intended": {"primary_class": "TECHNICAL_EXTENSION", "flags": [], "consequential": 1}, "injection": false, "expect_precheck": false, "notes": ""}
{"case_id": "bench-017", "set": "synthetic-bench", "category": "technical_extension", "provenance": "synthetic", "post_title": "What I learned migrating a monolith to Postgres 17", "parent": null, "reply_to_author": false, "body_html": "<p>For anyone doing this with logical replication, <a href=\"https://example.org/pg-sequences\">sequences are not replicated</a>, so sync them right before cutover.</p>", "body_source_format": "HTML", "intended": {"primary_class": "TECHNICAL_EXTENSION", "flags": [], "consequential": 1}, "injection": false, "expect_precheck": false, "notes": ""}
{"case_id": "bench-018", "set": "synthetic-bench", "category": "technical_extension", "provenance": "synthetic", "post_title": "Prompt templates as versioned config", "parent": null, "reply_to_author": false, "body_html": "<p>We store a hash of the rendered prompt next to every output. It made regressions after template edits much easier to find.</p>", "body_source_format": "HTML", "intended": {"primary_class": "TECHNICAL_EXTENSION", "flags": [], "consequential": 1}, "injection": false, "expect_precheck": false, "notes": ""}
